  "note": "Triennial election of the rural district councillors, polled on Thursday 2 June 1949. Only two divisions of the Antrim rural district were contested, Antrim Urban and Crumlin; polling in both was under the notices of poll of 19 May 1949. No party labels were printed except in the results. Two seats. One Unionist gain from Labour. Candidates as printed in the Antrim notice of poll (Belfast News-Letter, 20 May 1949, p. 3)."
